<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hibernia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ivernia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hibernia is the classical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> name for Ireland, related to Greek forms such as Ierne and Ptolemy's Iouernia, which derive from the same Celtic root as the Irish name Ériu. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> never conquered Ireland, though they traded with it, and the name was used in Latin texts through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hibernia.jpg" alt="Hibernia" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ireland_from_space_edit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
